-`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+`src/i18n/messages.js`; every error code has a message in both.
+
+The language comes from the request's `Accept-Language` header: the supported
+language with the highest q-value wins (the first one listed on a tie), and
+region tags count as their language (`ko-KR` is `ko`). Without the header, or
+when it names neither language (or only `*`), the server answers in
+`LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
